<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul applies for record bond issues for March.</title>
<headline>Seoul applies for record bond issues for March.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-backed Korea Securities Dealers Association said on Friday it received a record 3.91 trillion won worth of new corporate bond issue applications for March.</p>
<p>That compared with February's 2.91 trillion won, the association said in a statement.</p>
<p>The corporate yields briefly touched a high of 12.5 percent in early trading on Friday on expectations of huge new issues in March.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
